---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'What to Do When Your Payment Fails in China';
const description = 'Common payment failure reasons for foreign travelers in China and step-by-step troubleshooting when your QR code payment won\'t go through.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <a href="/en/payment/" class="text-sm text-brand-600 hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1 mb-4">← Payment</a>
      <div class="text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium tracking-wide uppercase mb-3">Payment</div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-4">
        What to Do When Your Payment Fails in China
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        It's going to happen at some point. You're at a shop, you scan the QR code, the app spins for a moment, and then — error. Payment failed.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Don't panic. Payment failures in China are common for foreign users, and most of the time it's a simple fix.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Why It Happened</h2>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-8">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-5 not-prose">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">1. You hit the daily limit</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Both Alipay Tour Pass and WeChat Pay have limits on how much you can spend. If you've been shopping, you might have hit the ceiling.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mt-2"><strong>Fix:</strong> Wait until the next day — daily limits reset. If you need more info on limits, check our <a href="/en/payment/setup-alipay/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Alipay</a> or <a href="/en/payment/setup-wechat/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">WeChat Pay</a> guides.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-5 not-prose">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">2. Your bank blocked the transaction</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Your bank sees a charge coming from China and thinks it's fraud.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mt-2"><strong>Fix:</strong> Check your notifications — your bank usually sends an SMS or push notification asking if it's you. Approve it and try again. For next time, notify your bank before you travel.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-5 not-prose">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">3. The merchant's WiFi is flaky</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Free WiFi in small shops can be slow or unstable.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mt-2"><strong>Fix:</strong> Switch to your mobile data. Most Chinese SIM cards and eSIMs have fast data, and paying over your own connection is more secure anyway.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-5 not-prose">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">4. The QR code expired</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Restaurants and chain stores often generate a new code for each order that has a time limit.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mt-2"><strong>Fix:</strong> Ask the server to generate a new QR code. Or try scanning again — sometimes it just needed a fresh attempt.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-5 not-prose">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">5. The merchant only accepts Chinese bank transfers</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Some small vendors, especially in rural areas or traditional markets, only accept payments from Chinese bank accounts. Your foreign card won't work here even through Alipay.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mt-2"><strong>Fix:</strong> Use cash. This is why we recommend keeping ¥100–200 in small bills on you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Step-by-Step: What to Do Right Now</h2>

      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-4 text-gray-700 mb-8">
        <li><strong>Don't keep trying</strong> — the same error will happen again. Stop and switch methods.</li>
        <li><strong>Check your balance</strong> — make sure you haven't hit a limit.</li>
        <li><strong>Try the other app</strong> — if Alipay failed, try WeChat Pay. If neither works...</li>
        <li><strong>Pull out cash</strong> — this is why you carry cash.</li>
        <li><strong>Ask the merchant</strong> — show them your phone and say "不能付" (<em>bù néng fù</em> — "can't pay"). They might try scanning your QR code instead.</li>
        <li><strong>Connect to your own data</strong> — if you were on WiFi, switch to mobile data.</li>
      </ol>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Proactive Things You Can Do</h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Before you leave for China:</p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <li>Set up both <a href="/en/payment/setup-alipay/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Alipay</a> and <a href="/en/payment/setup-wechat/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">WeChat Pay</a> (two is safer than one)</li>
        <li>Withdraw ¥500–1000 in cash from an ATM after you arrive</li>
        <li>Download your bank's app so you can approve transactions quickly</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        If you've tried everything and still can't pay, find the nearest <strong>Bank of China</strong> ATM — they're usually the most foreigner-friendly — and withdraw more cash. Then sort out the app issue later at your hotel.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <div class="bg-brand-50 border border-brand-100 rounded-2xl p-6 not-prose">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Related guides</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li><a href="/en/payment/payment-guide/" class="text-sm text-brand-600 hover:underline">Back to the payment overview →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/en/payment/foreign-cards/" class="text-sm text-brand-600 hover:underline">Using foreign credit cards in China →</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
